2:["$","div",null,{"className":"x:mx-auto x:flex x:max-w-(--nextra-content-width)","children":["$","$L18",null,{"value":[{"value":"The Starting Point","id":"the-starting-point","depth":2},{"value":"What I Used AI For","id":"what-i-used-ai-for","depth":2},{"value":"Codebase Exploration","id":"codebase-exploration","depth":3},{"value":"Markdown Instruction Files","id":"markdown-instruction-files","depth":3},{"value":"MCP Server Integration","id":"mcp-server-integration","depth":3},{"value":"Reusable Skills for Repeated Tasks","id":"reusable-skills-for-repeated-tasks","depth":3},{"value":"Documentation Consistency Review","id":"documentation-consistency-review","depth":3},{"value":"Embedded Payment Page Widget","id":"embedded-payment-page-widget","depth":3},{"value":"Accessibility Audit","id":"accessibility-audit","depth":3},{"value":"Information Architecture Overhaul","id":"information-architecture-overhaul","depth":3},{"value":"The CI/CD Pipeline","id":"the-cicd-pipeline","depth":2},{"value":"What AI Changed","id":"what-ai-changed","depth":2},{"value":"What AI Didn’t Change","id":"what-ai-didnt-change","depth":2},{"value":"What I’d Tell Someone Starting Out","id":"what-id-tell-someone-starting-out","depth":2}],"children":[["$","$L19",null,{}],["$","$L1a",null,{"metadata":{"title":"How I Integrated AI into a Documentation Workflow and What It Actually Changed","filePath":"content/portfolio/ai-documentation-workflow.mdx","timestamp":1775577541000},"bottomContent":"$undefined","sourceCode":"$undefined","children":[["$","div",null,{"id":"nextra-skip-nav"}],["$","main",null,{"data-pagefind-body":true,"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"portfolio-post","children":[["$","h1",null,{"id":"$undefined","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-bold x:mt-2 x:text-4xl","children":["How I Integrated AI into a Documentation Workflow and What It Actually Changed","$undefined"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"AI tools are everywhere in documentation conversations right now, but most of the discussion stays abstract. “Use AI to write faster.” “AI will transform technical writing.” That kind of thing."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"This is a concrete account of how I integrated AI into the documentation workflow at Orbital, a fintech payments company, where I was the sole technical writer managing three products, 40+ API endpoints, and a growing knowledge base on ReadMe."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"What I used it for. How I structured that use. What it measurably changed about how I worked."}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"the-starting-point","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border","children":["The Starting Point",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"the-starting-point"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"When I joined Orbital, the documentation was fragmented across platforms, outdated, and didn’t reflect the current product. I was rebuilding the entire system while the product team kept shipping. Three products (Merchant Payments API, Global Payments API, Client Portal), 75+ knowledge base pages to create, and 40+ API endpoints to migrate from Postman into ReadMe."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"The surface area was large and I was one person. The question wasn’t whether AI could help. It was whether it could help in ways that were reliable enough to trust and repeatable enough to build a workflow around."}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"what-i-used-ai-for","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border","children":["What I Used AI For",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"what-i-used-ai-for"}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"codebase-exploration","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Codebase Exploration",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"codebase-exploration"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"One of the hardest parts of documenting a payments API is understanding what the code actually does. I used Claude Code to explore the Orbital codebase, understand endpoint behaviour, and surface what I needed to write accurately about a feature before drafting anything."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"This wasn’t about generating documentation from code. It was about compressing the research phase. When you’re migrating 40+ endpoints from Postman into ReadMe, you need to understand every parameter, every response schema, every edge case. Claude helped me get to a working understanding of complex payment flows faster than reading the code alone."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"For example, when documenting the hosted payment page (HPP) integration, I used Claude to trace the full request lifecycle through the codebase, understand what headers were required, what the response object looked like at each stage, and where the error states were. That research would have taken a full day manually. With Claude, I had the technical foundation in a couple of hours, and I could spend the rest of the day writing the actual documentation."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"markdown-instruction-files","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Markdown Instruction Files",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"markdown-instruction-files"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":["I created structured markdown files that gave AI assistants context about the documentation project: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"nextra-code","dir":"ltr","children":"skills.md"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"className":"nextra-code","dir":"ltr","children":"agents.md"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"className":"nextra-code","dir":"ltr","children":"prompts.md"}],". These files described the tone, the architecture, the terminology, and the conventions for the Orbital documentation."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"This meant that every time I started a Claude Code session or worked with Gemini, the AI wasn’t guessing. It had a shared understanding of what “good” looked like for this specific project. The ReadMe style conventions, the API documentation format, the way we structured knowledge base articles versus API reference pages."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"Together, these meant any AI session working on Orbital docs started from a shared foundation, and any future writer picking up these tools would get consistent results."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"mcp-server-integration","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["MCP Server Integration",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"mcp-server-integration"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"I connected MCP servers to give AI tools direct access to the live documentation. This was the real unlock."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"Instead of copying and pasting content into a chat window, the AI could read the actual published docs on ReadMe and generate content that was consistent with what was already there. When you’re maintaining 75+ knowledge base pages across three products, consistency is the hard part. Not the writing itself, but making sure the webhooks guide doesn’t contradict the authentication guide, and the Client Portal docs use the same terminology as the API docs."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"reusable-skills-for-repeated-tasks","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Reusable Skills for Repeated Tasks",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"reusable-skills-for-repeated-tasks"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"For tasks I performed repeatedly, like auditing new endpoints against the existing documentation structure, or generating the initial scaffold for a new knowledge base article, I created reusable skills that codified the process."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"Rather than re-explaining the task each session, the skill carried the context, structure, and steps. This had a compounding effect: as I refined a skill, every future use of it got better. It also meant the workflow was transferable. If another writer joined the team, they wouldn’t need to reverse-engineer my process."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"documentation-consistency-review","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Documentation Consistency Review",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"documentation-consistency-review"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"I used AI to audit the existing documentation for consistency against our internal style guide. Claude could quickly flag terminology drift, formatting inconsistencies, and tone mismatches at a scale that would have taken weeks to do manually."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"When you’re unifying three separate products into one documentation experience, consistency across every page matters. The Merchant Payments API docs needed to feel like they belonged on the same site as the Client Portal knowledge base. AI made it possible to audit the full doc set and catch the small inconsistencies that a human reviewer would miss on pass 47."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"embedded-payment-page-widget","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Embedded Payment Page Widget",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"embedded-payment-page-widget"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"One of the features the documentation needed was an embedded payment page demo. Rather than waiting on engineering cycles, I used Claude Code to prototype the widget implementation, including the front-end integration and the documentation that would accompany it. The result was a working prototype that engineering could refine rather than build from the ground up, and documentation that was ready before the feature shipped."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"accessibility-audit","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Accessibility Audit",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"accessibility-audit"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"I used Claude to audit the ReadMe documentation site for accessibility issues. This included identifying missing alt text, checking colour contrast ratios, verifying keyboard navigation paths, and flagging heading hierarchy problems across the documentation. The audit surfaced issues that would have taken weeks to find manually, and the fixes improved the experience for all users, not just those relying on assistive technology."}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"information-architecture-overhaul","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl","children":["Information Architecture Overhaul",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"information-architecture-overhaul"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"The most ambitious project was the complete restructuring of how documentation was organised across the three products. When I joined, each product’s documentation existed in isolation. The information architecture needed to unify them into a single coherent experience while still making it easy for a merchant integrating only one product to find what they needed."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"I used Claude throughout this project to evaluate structural options, pressure-test navigation logic, and draft the new architecture. With 75+ pages to organise, categorise, and cross-link, AI proved invaluable for exploring different approaches quickly and identifying gaps in coverage."}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"the-cicd-pipeline","className":"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border","children":["The CI/CD Pipeline",["$","$L1b",null,{"id":"the-cicd-pipeline"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":"Beyond AI-powered writing workflows, I built the infrastructure that kept the documentation accurate. I set up CI/CD pipelines with GitHub Actions that automated the repetitive checks:"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Automated linting and formatting:"}],"\nEvery pull request ran through automated checks for markdown formatting, consistent heading styles, and proper link syntax. This caught the class of errors that neither humans nor AI are good at catching consistently."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Link checking:"}],"\nBroken links erode trust. The pipeline checked every internal and external link on every PR, flagging anything that 404’d before it could reach production."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Spell checking:"}],"\nWith fintech-specific terminology (PSP, HPP, EPP, KYC, AML), the spell checker needed a custom dictionary. I configured it to understand Orbital’s domain vocabulary without flagging every acronym as a typo."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:leading-7","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"OpenAPI spec sync with ReadMe:"}],"\nThis was the most impactful automation. I configured GitHub Actions to sync the OpenAPI specification with ReadMe so the API reference automatically regenerated whenever the spec file changed. This meant the API docs were never out of sync with the actual API. Before this, spec updates required manual re-uploading to ReadMe, and the docs were frequently stale."]}],["$","div",null,{"data-pagefind-ignore":"all","className":"nextra-code x:relative x:not-first:mt-[1.25em]","children":["$undefined",["$","pre",null,{"className":"x:group x:focus-visible:nextra-focus x:overflow-x-auto x:subpixel-antialiased x:text-[.9em] x:bg-white x:dark:bg-black x:py-4 x:ring-1 x:ring-inset x:ring-gray-300 x:dark:ring-neutral-700 x:contrast-more:ring-gray-900 x:contrast-more:dark:ring-gray-50 x:contrast-more:contrast-150 x:rounded-md not-prose","tabIndex":"0","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"x:group-hover:opacity-100 x:group-focus:opacity-100 x:opacity-0 x:transition x:focus-within:opacity-100 x:flex x:gap-1 x:absolute x:right-4 x:top-2","children":[["$","$L1c",null,{"children":["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","height":"1em","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M4 19h6v-2H4v2zM20 5H4v2h16V5zm-3 6H4v2h13.25c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2s-.9 2-2 2H15v-2l-3 3l3 3v-2h2c2.21 0 4-1.79 4-4s-1.79-4-4-4z"}]}]}],false]}],["$","code",null,{"className":"nextra-code","dir":"ltr","children